  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb (す ending, conjugates as s-row: {着|き}こなさない, {着|き}こなします). Transitive — takes a clothing item marked with を.\n\nUSAGE:\n{着|き}こなす emphasizes skill and style in wearing clothes, not just the act of putting them on. It is commonly used in fashion contexts to praise someone's ability to make any outfit look good.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- スーツを{着|き}こなす (to wear a suit well)\n- {和服|わふく}を{着|き}こなす (to wear kimono stylishly)\n- {上手|じょうず}に{着|き}こなす (to dress well)\n- おしゃれに{着|き}こなす (to wear fashionably)",
